{"name":"Robin’s Pride","hex":"#abc3ca","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"robin","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various passerine birds (about 100 species) of the families Muscicapidae, Turdidae and Petroicidae (formerly Eopsaltriidae), typically with a red breast.\n A European robin, Erithacus rubecula.\n\n An American robin, Turdus migratorius.","A European robin, Erithacus rubecula."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A toxalbumin obtained from the locust tree."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/robin"},{"term":"pride","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The quality or state of being proud.\nA sense of one's own worth; reasonable self-esteem and satisfaction (in oneself, in one's work, one's family, etc).","A sense of one's own worth; reasonable self-esteem and satisfaction (in oneself, in one's work, one's family, etc)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To take or experience pride in something; to be proud of it."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pride"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pride","blocks":[{"text":"Pride is a primary emotion characterized by a sense of security with one's identity, performance, and/or accomplishments. Depending on the context, pride may be viewed as either a virtue or a vice. Typically, pride arises from praise, independent self-reflection, or a fulfilled feeling of belonging."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Pride_%28Superbia%29%2C_from_The_Seven_Vices_MET_DP867537.jpg/330px-Pride_%28Superbia%29%2C_from_The_Seven_Vices_MET_DP867537.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pride"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Pride%2C_Jacob_Matham.png/250px-Pride%2C_Jacob_Matham.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/29/Pride%2C_Jacob_M